    dcterm:references cx:engEME_TheFVIconstruction_Sources ;
    rcxn:annotator membr:Tzimas .

cx:engEME_TheFVIconstruction_Meaning a rcxn:ConstructionMeaning ;
    rcxn:hasMeaning "FVI is an information-packaging device. It (mostly) makes sure that information structure abides by the Given-before-New and Ground-before-Figure principles. It is also genre-dependent: in narrative contexts it is also found to serve linking-to-previous-discourse functions  and acts as a focusing device." .

